          "text": "The pattern indexes as an **orthorhombic C-centered cell**, with the diagnostic series \\(020\\), \\(040\\), \\(060\\), and \\(080\\). The resulting structure is the **CrB/TlI-type oC8 structure**, space group **Cmcm (No. 63)**, with four CeMg formula units per conventional cell.\n\nRepresentative indexing:\n\n| Observed 2\u03b8 (\u00b0) | hkl |\n|---:|:---:|\n| 14.92 | 020 |\n| 30.11 | 040 |\n| 33.68 | 111 |\n| 34.83 | 130 |\n| 39.11 | 002 |\n| 42.08 | 022 |\n| 45.86 | 060 |\n| 53.42 | 132 |\n| 61.71 | 062 |\n| 62.55 | 080 |\n| 70.82 | 222 |\n| 73.52 | 260 |\n\nThe lattice parameters are well constrained by the peak positions. The internal \\(y\\) coordinates are less precise without a full instrumental-profile Rietveld refinement and should be regarded as approximate.\n\n```cif\ndata_CeMg\n_audit_creation_method              'Structure solution from supplied Cu Kalpha1 powder pattern'\n_chemical_name_common               'cerium magnesium'\n_chemical_formula_sum               'Ce Mg'\n_chemical_formula_structural        'CeMg'\n_cell_formula_units_Z               4\n\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt           'C m c m'\n_space_group_name_Hall              '-C 2c 2'\n_space_group_IT_number              63\n\n_cell_length_a                      3.3892\n_cell_length_b                     11.8647\n_cell_length_c                      4.6021\n_cell_angle_alpha                  90\n_cell_angle_beta                   90\n_cell_angle_gamma                  90\n_cell_volume                       185.06\n\n_exptl_crystal_density_diffrn       5.90\n_diffrn_radiation_probe             x-ray\n_diffrn_radiation_type              'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength        1.5406\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_B_iso_or_equiv\nCe1 Ce 4 c 0.00000 0.1670 0.25000 1.000 0.50\nMg1 Mg 4 c 0.00000 0.4250 0.25000 1.000 0.50\n```\n\nEquivalent origin choices, such as replacing a listed \\(y\\) by \\(1-y\\), describe the same structure. The **Cmcm cell and CrB/TlI-type topology are the robust part of the solution**; the two positional parameters should be refined against the full profile before publication.",
